<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S6.T1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 6.1</span>: </span><span id="S6.T1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Average number of cache line probes for hash tables. Load probes measure average #probes per operation as the tables are loaded to 90% load factor. Aging probes measure average number of probes over 1000 iterations of the aging benchmark. <sup id="S6.T1.6.1" class="ltx_sup">∗</sup> values do not use locks, which artificially lowers their probe count.</span></figcaption>
